1	//! The durable agent-loop Temporal workflow.
2	//!
3	//! [`DurableAgentWorkflow`] is a **mechanical executor** of
4	//! [`crate::driver::DurableDriver`]: it owns no agent logic of its own. It
5	//! loops `driver.next_effect()` and satisfies each requested
6	//! [`crate::driver::DriverEffect`] with a Temporal activity
7	//! ([`crate::activities`]'s `render_instructions` / `call_model` /
8	//! `invoke_tool`), feeding the activity result back through the matching
9	//! `apply_*` method. The whole loop is raced against a durable run-deadline
10	//! timer and cooperative workflow cancellation; both interruptions call
11	//! [`crate::driver::DurableDriver::interrupt`] and return a normal
12	//! [`crate::payloads::DurableRunOutcome`] (finalize-on-every-exit).
13	//!
14	//! # Determinism
15	//!
16	//! Everything in this module runs inside the Temporal workflow sandbox, so it
17	//! must be deterministic across replay: no wall-clock time, no `uuid`, no
18	//! randomness, and no `HashMap` **iteration** (a single keyed
19	//! [`std::collections::HashMap::get`] by `WorkflowInput::agent_name` is
20	//! deterministic and is the only map access performed here). The workflow's
21	//! own decision-making is entirely delegated to `core::transition` (via the
22	//! driver); concurrency and timers use the SDK's deterministic
23	//! [`temporalio_sdk::workflows::join_all`] / durable-timer primitives.
24	//!
25	//! # Registry closure (how the plan reaches the workflow)
26	//!
27	//! An [`crate::driver::AgentPlan`] must **never** be serialized (its
28	//! `OutputType` validator fails closed after a round-trip — see
29	//! [`crate::activities::DurableAgentDef`]). The workflow therefore resolves
30	//! its plan from a **process-local**, `Ctx`-free
31	//! `HashMap<String, AgentPlan>` closed over by the workflow factory:
32	//! [`crate::worker::TemporalAgentWorkerBuilder::build`] derives that map from
33	//! its `Ctx`-generic agent registry and passes it (plus the per-activity
34	//! [`temporalio_sdk::ActivityOptions`]) into [`build_activity_config`], whose
35	//! [`WorkflowActivityConfig`] the `register_workflow_with_factory` closure
36	//! clones into each [`DurableAgentWorkflow`] instance. `AgentPlan` is `Ctx`-
37	//! free, so the workflow struct needs no `Ctx` type parameter.
38	
39	use std::collections::HashMap;
40	use std::sync::Arc;
41	use std::time::Duration;
42	
43	use futures_util::FutureExt as _;
44	use paigasus_helikon_core::{TokenUsage, ToolCallOutcome, ToolCallRequest};
45	use temporalio_common::protos::temporal::api::common::v1::RetryPolicy;
46	use temporalio_macros::{workflow, workflow_methods};
47	use temporalio_sdk::{ActivityExecutionError, ActivityOptions, WorkflowContext, WorkflowResult};
48	
49	use crate::activities::AgentActivities;
50	use crate::driver::{AgentPlan, DriverEffect, DurableDriver, InterruptKind};
51	use crate::error::ErrorKindPayload;
52	use crate::payloads::{DurableRunOutcome, RunStatusPayload, WorkflowInput};
53	use crate::worker::RetryPolicyConfig;
